e we continue i'd like to give a  shout out to the sponsors of this video  alchemy stars alchemy stars is a hero  collector game that takes you to the  beautiful world of aurora a realm where  science and magic cross having spent  some time on the game i'd say that i  immediately fell in love with the art  the character designs are my jam and  there's nothing more addictive than  having these heroes join your ranks and  growing stronger along with them even  though i'm not rolling for units and  collecting my favorites i'd like to  bring your attention to the unique grid  based gameplay of alchemy stars here let  me give you a demo of the strategic  intricacies that goes into every battle  in this game this isn't your typical  grid based strategy game as you need to  bring your a-game every time to win the  battles in the grandest way possible  take advantage of those coloured tiles  in order to lead your team to unleash  destruction upon your foes as more  stages open up you'll have to learn not  to only optimize your units and attack  chains but also deal with various stage  gimmicks and hazards that hamper your  quest the game is set for release this  summer it won't be long now and i hope  that i can see you in the fields of  aurora soon i can help you get started  with a link in my description box so  what are you waiting for check the link  in the description and download now  let's take a look at one piece now shall  we specifically sanji vs judge not too  long ago in one piece standards we've  got another epic father-son battle to  add to the gauntlet with sanji finally  getting his hands on his father who he's  not on good terms with and that's  putting it lightly sanji hates his  neglectful and abusive father and that  all comes to a boiling point when they  finally battle each other the two had a  back and forth duel after sanji  reaffirms his convictions empowered by  unpleasant memories of his youth sanji  manages a furious recovery however he  gets caught off guard by his father's  soldiers and that's what leads to his  defeat from a storyline perspective it  would make sense at that point of the  story but i personally want to see him  break through those walls soon i think  that eventually we could potentially see  him overcome that final hurdle and  complete his character arc  [Music]  since we're on the topic of classic  anime let's continue with yusuke versus  ryzen among the numerous arcs of yuu  hakusho the three kings arc is one of  the less renowned ones and that doesn't  mean that it's devoid of some key  moments and memorable fights however one  such fight is the battle between yusuke  and his ancestral father ryzen after the  appetizer of a battle yusuke and his  team go on to meet ryzen for their  battle it could have been a mistake on  yusuke's part as he gets absolutely  trounced in this battle despite all that  yusuke's been through in terms of  becoming stronger he still realizes that  his father's strength far surpasses his  despite the father not even being in  peak form this pushes yusuke into a  training arc only to be disappointed  when it's time for the rematch despite  ryzen nearly killing yusuke in their  second meeting the former simply  explained some important revelations to  his son before shortly dying due to  starvation yet such a shame we never got  to see the fight between father and son  when they're at their peak powers now  isn't it then again who are we kidding  ryzen's probably going to run away with  it considering how pig ryzen is and is  probably the strongest being in the yu  yu hakusho universe  we move on from that one to the next  battle gara versus rasa the battle of  sand wielders is one of the early  highlights in naruto's fourth shinobi  war reincarnated by garbudo rasa gets  sent to fight the allied shinobi forces  it's just fitting that his major  bachelor would be in the form of a duel  with his own son gaara and rasa was just  a thing of beauty and a great battle  between two sandbenders so to speak it's  a battle that makes it seem that the  father is in control throughout and he  moves on to finish the job with the  techniques he's used to defeat the one  tail however though to his surprise he  realizes too late that his son is no  longer who he once was realizing some  regrets as a parent rasa finally  succumbs and gets resealed after a  climactic scene but before doing so  however he gets to share a very tender  moment with his son where he  congratulates the latter and expresses  his apologies  [Music]  next in line is goku vs gohan  how could we not include probably the  most iconic father-son duo in anime goku  and gohan had a lot of history and my  favorite among those moments besides the  passing of the torch way back in the  cell saga is the dragon ball super fight  in a bid to become stronger gohan passes  on more training with piccolo in order  to have a more challenging test a tag  fight just doesn't do it so gohan  proposes an all-out battle against his  father goku in super saiyan 2 is already  a humongous challenge to have in front  of you but gohan just knows no backing  down and still manages to keep pace this  forces goku to bring out super saiyan  blue which gohan responds to by powering  up even more at the end of the clash  goku reigns supreme but gohan more than  earned some newfound respect from his  father i think the fight with its  responses of power-ups and display of  sheer destruction helps encapsulate why  a lot of people love dragon ball so much  the cool thing about the fight is that  it's not just a battle of strength it's  gohan's attempt to showing the fruits of  his growth and the reaffirmation of his  vow to keep pushing himself and his  father to greater heights among the  father-son fights in anime i think the  few can come close to the emotional  stakes of gray versus silver  it's been a long time coming and with  the culmination of fairy tale at hand  it's only right for gray to finally have  his long fated showdown against his  father who's long believed to be dead  it's the battle of two top tier ice  wielders in fairy tale and it's just  full of hype i know fairy tales been  notorious for some of its fights but i  think that the fight between gray and  silva is one that didn't disappoint as  expected from two people who know each  other's moves very well the fight ended  up being touch and go with both fighters  countering each other's moves silver  gets the upper hand for a stretch but  powered by his resolve and memories of  the past gray wins after some clever  bluffing in the technique vambrace i  like this fight because it feels like  the culmination of grey's backstory that  started all the way to the second arc of  the series it camps off a long journey  on a plot point that i honestly think  that the author had forgotten but we did  get some closure and some feels along  the way  [Music]  history stems from way back they've  never been each other's best friends  ever since the time kamui was much  younger and it all came ahead towards  the end of the rakuyo decisive battle  arc the sudden appearance of kamui  sparks a battle between father and son  and you can just feel all the pent-up  emotions overflow with each move they do  for kamui it's a battle of redemption a  way for him to prove that he's come a  long way and has become far stronger  than his father could imagine the fight  was looking like something that would  end when one of the two die but gagura  manages to stop the battle and appeal to  their familial bonds  so that's it for today pretty much a  video befitting the occasion of father's  day everyone if you're up for more  special videos like this please comment  with your suggestions otherwise feel  free to talk about other stuff like your  favorite father-son duos in anime if you  enjoyed the video which i sure hope you  did don't forget to drop a like and  maybe share the video and the channel to  your friends yo